[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://assets/bonelight/ui/spells/stormsweep-lightning.png" id="3_icon"]

; An arc of storm-light swept beside the player on the side he faces, aimed at nothing
; (scripts/Stormsweep.cs).
;
; BaseDamage is ONE SWEEP, on everything it passes over. BaseProjectileCount is the sweeps one cooldown
; casts, in sequence 0.14 s apart: the first to the facing side, the second to the other, and so on.
; BaseRange is the arc's reach from the player's centre (px); the band it sweeps is
; Stormsweep.BaseHalfBand (22 px) above and below him plus the AreaSize lines below (Effect 7, in px).
; The player's Area and every milestone's AreaMultiplier scale both the reach and the band.
;
; Written out in full so Player.EnsureRelevantLevelUps generates nothing of its own: every level adds
; damage, even levels take the cooldown step every spell gets, level 2 adds the sweep to the other
; side and level 8 a third, odd levels from 3 thicken the band, and 4 and 7 lengthen it. Level 8:
; 21 damage, 3 sweeps every 1.08 s, a 190 px arc over a 60 px band.

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_stormsweep_lvl2"]
